/**
 * The paywall config: schema, parsing and validation.
 *
 * This file is the security boundary of the gateway. `endpoints` is an
 * ALLOWLIST — a path that does not match an entry is never proxied, never
 * priced, and never reaches the upstream. Getting the matching wrong exposes
 * an upstream the operator believed was private, so the matcher below is
 * deliberately dull: literal segments and a single trailing `*`, no regex, no
 * backtracking, no user-supplied patterns compiled at runtime.
 *
 * Validation fails LOUDLY and completely. A merchant config is authored once
 * and then serves money; a silently-ignored typo (`prise:` for `price:`) would
 * mean an endpoint served free, so unknown keys are errors rather than being
 * dropped.
 */
